Z||000002||moonie||07-25-2000||09:40 AM||||<BR>if i don't get my 85 SE 4cyl fixxed soon , it may very well be for sale. i love fiero's ( this is my second one ) but i am NOT a mechanic & it looks like you pretty much have to be to own one. <P>It looks good sitting in the driveway though !!<BR>LOL <P>moonster<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||07-25-2000||09:51 AM||||<BR>moonie, welcome to the forum, it's good to have another Pontiac Fiero Freak (PFF - get it) amongst the proud group.<P>btw, you don't have to believe that you are mechanically inclined to begin work on your car, you just have to believe in yourself and be willing to take the opportunity to learn and purchase some tools  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Addtionally, if you have not already done so, purchase the Chilton repair manual for the Fiero, and the Haynes repair manual for the Fiero. Both are good sources for basic maintenance and how-to's, and both are available at most auto parts stores.<P>Next, if you have a question or problem, submit it to the fine folks here at PFF, someone, somewhere has been through your identified problem.  Just one note regarding submitting your problems, depending on the problem, make sure to give the engine and tranny combination, this helps in narrowing down problems.<P>Again, welcome, and good luck.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
